// Title: Removal Of AMSI Provider Registry Keys
// ID: 41d1058a-aea7-4952-9293-29eaaf516465
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2021-06-07
// Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
// Description: Detects the deletion of AMSI provider registry key entries in HKLM\Software\Microsoft\AMSI. This technique could be used by an attacker in order to disable AMSI inspection.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

source = logs-* | where (((registry.path="*{2781761E-28E0-4109-99FE-B9D127C57AFE}" OR registry.path="*{A7C452EF-8E9F-42EB-9F2B-245613CA0DC9}")) AND NOT (((process.executable="C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Platform\\*" OR process.executable="C:\\Program Files\\Windows Defender\\*" OR process.executable="C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Windows Defender\\*") AND process.executable="*\\MsMpEng.exe")))
